cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Varion (AI_DNA_ANALYZER): statistical SNP calling (R2) and indel calling (nindels, R3.1), research software"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mark
    family-names: Kostogryzov
repository-code: "https://github.com/krmox/AI_DNA_ANALYZER"
# `doi` is the Zenodo concept DOI (all versions; resolves to the latest version). The
# version-specific DOI of release 3.1.0 is listed under `identifiers`. The Zenodo archive of
# tag 3.0.0 (10.5281/zenodo.23855773) does NOT contain R3.1.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22895745
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23856530
    description: "Zenodo version DOI of Varion 3.1.0 (archive of tag 3.1.0)"
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/krmox/AI_DNA_ANALYZER/releases/tag/3.1.0"
    description: "GitHub release 3.1.0"
version: 3.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-03
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genomics
  - variant calling
  - SNP
  - indel
  - Genome in a Bottle
  - hap.py
  - htslib
abstract: >-
  Research germline variant calling software for Illumina short reads (GRCh38).
  The SNP engine (R2) combines a binomial screen, a per-read Poisson-binomial model
  and a logistic classifier with frozen constants. The indel engine (nindels) scores
  candidate indels with a banded PairHMM, with optional joint multi-allelic
  genotyping and a repeat-specific error model. Release 3.1.0 adds a front-end
  command and a depth-dependent choice between two indel configurations whose
  frozen thresholds deviate from the pre-registered protocol (see
  docs/R3.1_THRESHOLD_SELECTION.md). Evaluated on a small number of GIAB samples and
  chromosomes; not a production or clinical caller.
